CORE
read_through.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ addresses of constant members: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [basic.def.odr]/4, [basic.start.static]/2: a constexpr (or const)
static data member whose address is taken is an object with static
storage duration initialized with its value; reading through the pointer
yields the value.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept the program.  Fails on
bin53.
